Building this package clones open62541pp (and its open62541 dependency)
during the CMake configure step via FetchContent. debian/rules turns
off FETCHCONTENT_FULLY_DISCONNECTED (which dh would otherwise set) so
that clone can happen. The build therefore needs network access, git
and ca-certificates.

Sphinx HTML documentation is built with the system python3-sphinx and
python3-sphinx-rtd-theme (not docs/.venv) and installed under
/usr/share/doc/trigaserver/html/. Pass nodoc in DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS to
skip that step.

trigaserver-doc.service starts a dedicated Apache (apache2-bin) on
port 8080 serving that HTML. Both that unit and trigaserver.service
are enabled and started on install.

Example:

  sudo apt install build-essential debhelper devscripts
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

If you use sbuild or pbuilder, allow network during the build.
The resulting .deb is written to the parent directory of the source tree.
